; Reverse outer traversal: per-row scale with a decreasing outer IV. The
; GEPs are inbounds and adjacent outer iterations write disjoint rows, so
; the adjacent-iteration check can succeed; but the outer stride is
; negative, so the inbounds-shortcut that skips the monotonicity check is
; unsound. Without a sound monotonicity proof, non-adjacent iterations are
; not known to be disjoint.
;
;   for (i = N-1; i >= 0; i--)
;     for (j = 0; j < M; j++)
